  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In GIMP, when creating a 3D depth effect on text using duplicate layers, if you offset the lower layer horizontally by \(5\) pixels, how does it affect the illusion of thickness?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "It increases the perceived depth or thickness by \\(5\\) units along the X-axis", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "It changes the overall image resolution from RGB to grayscale", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It automatically crops the canvas to fit the main text boundary", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It deletes the alpha channel from the active layer mask", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L2: Graphics in ICT"]', '["gimp", "3d_effect", "coordinates", "ict_level2"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In GIMP, when creating a 3D depth effect on text using duplicate layers, if you offset the lower layer horizontally by \(10\) pixels, how does it affect the illusion of thickness?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "It increases the perceived depth or thickness by \\(10\\) units along the X-axis", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "It changes the overall image resolution from RGB to grayscale", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It automatically crops the canvas to fit the main text boundary", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It deletes the alpha channel from the active layer mask", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L2: Graphics in ICT"]', '["gimp", "3d_effect", "coordinates", "ict_level2"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In GIMP, when creating a 3D depth effect on text using duplicate layers, if you offset the lower layer horizontally by \(15\) pixels, how does it affect the illusion of thickness?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "It increases the perceived depth or thickness by \\(15\\) units along the X-axis", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "It changes the overall image resolution from RGB to grayscale", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It automatically crops the canvas to fit the main text boundary", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It deletes the alpha channel from the active layer mask", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L2: Graphics in ICT"]', '["gimp", "3d_effect", "coordinates", "ict_level2"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In GIMP, when creating a 3D depth effect on text using duplicate layers, if you offset the lower layer horizontally by \(20\) pixels, how does it affect the illusion of thickness?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "It increases the perceived depth or thickness by \\(20\\) units along the X-axis", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "It changes the overall image resolution from RGB to grayscale", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It automatically crops the canvas to fit the main text boundary", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It deletes the alpha channel from the active layer mask", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L2: Graphics in ICT"]', '["gimp", "3d_effect", "coordinates", "ict_level2"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In GIMP, when creating a 3D depth effect on text using duplicate layers, if you offset the lower layer horizontally by \(25\) pixels, how does it affect the illusion of thickness?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "It increases the perceived depth or thickness by \\(25\\) units along the X-axis", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "It changes the overall image resolution from RGB to grayscale", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It automatically crops the canvas to fit the main text boundary", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It deletes the alpha channel from the active layer mask", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L2: Graphics in ICT"]', '["gimp", "3d_effect", "coordinates", "ict_level2"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In GIMP, when creating a 3D depth effect on text using duplicate layers, if you offset the lower layer horizontally by \(30\) pixels, how does it affect the illusion of thickness?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "It increases the perceived depth or thickness by \\(30\\) units along the X-axis", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "It changes the overall image resolution from RGB to grayscale", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It automatically crops the canvas to fit the main text boundary", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It deletes the alpha channel from the active layer mask", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L2: Graphics in ICT"]', '["gimp", "3d_effect", "coordinates", "ict_level2"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In the Level 2 curriculum, which operation represents a highly complex calculation?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Logical decision matching with a dynamic threshold formula", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Typing a basic text sentence in the text editor", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Using the fill tool to color a simple rectangle", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Clicking the green flag to run a move step script", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L2: Fundamentals of Computer"]', '["math", "auto", "ict_level2"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'An online meeting is a virtual gathering of people using the internet and video conferencing tools instead of meeting in person. Which of the following is an open-source meeting tool mentioned in the textbook?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Jitsi Meet", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Zoom", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Google Meet", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Skype", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["online_meetings", "open_source", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'To maintain a respectful and focused online meeting environment, which of the following is a key rule of etiquette recommended in the textbook?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Mute your microphone when you are not speaking", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Keep your video camera off at all times", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Send direct chat messages to every participant continuously", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Always keep your microphone unmuted to show active listening", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["online_meetings", "etiquette", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'An online workspace is a collection of cloud-based tools and apps that help people create, communicate, and collaborate online. Which of the following is an open-source online workspace tool option listed in the textbook?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Nextcloud Forms", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Google Workspace", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Microsoft 365", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Dropbox", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["online_workspace", "tools", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'Each tool in an online workspace has a specific purpose. If a student wants to make quizzes, surveys, and forms to collect organized information from people, which tool should they use?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Forms", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Docs", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Sheets", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Slides", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["online_workspace", "purpose", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'When creating a feedback or survey form, what setting must you enable if a SATS Number or email address question is mandatory and cannot be skipped by respondents?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Toggle the \\\"Required\\\" button at the bottom of the question box", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Select the \\\"Short answer\\\" option from the question type dropdown", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Change the color theme of the form in the customize menu", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Export the form to Sheets before sharing", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["online_workspace", "forms", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'How does an online file storage system like Google Drive or ownCloud assist students in online study and group work?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "It allows students to store documents, photos, and videos online safely and access or share them easily anytime from any device", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "It functions as a video editing software to create animations", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It is a database management tool that automatically generates mathematical graphs", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It is a software compiler that translates Python code into binary", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["online_workspace", "drive", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'When signed into YouTube, which specific user interface icon must a student click in the upper-right corner to upload a video from their device?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The camera icon with a plus sign (\\+)", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The notification bell icon", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The search magnifying glass icon", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The profile picture thumbnail icon", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["social_media", "youtube_upload", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'What does the term 3D stand for, and what are the three dimensions associated with 3D objects?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Three-Dimensional; objects have Length \\(X\\), Height \\(Y\\), and Depth \\(Z\\)", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Three-Digital; objects have width, height, and color channels", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Three-Directional; objects can only move left, right, and up", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Triple-Drawn; objects are drawn on paper three times to show shadows", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["3d_graphics", "dimensions", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'What is the primary visual difference between flat 2D text and 3D text?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "3D text has the illusion of thickness and depth, appearing raised or standing out in space, while 2D text is completely flat", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "2D text can be rotated and shaded, while 3D text is restricted to a single flat angle", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "3D text is always written in capital letters, while 2D text is written in lowercase", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "2D text is saved as a digital image, while 3D text can only exist on physical printed paper", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["3d_graphics", "text", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'Animation is based on a principle of human vision where a series of static images are shown very quickly in sequence to create the illusion of movement. What is each individual still image in an animation sequence called?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "A frame", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "A layer", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "A mask", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "A keyframe", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["animation", "concepts", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'What is the primary difference between Traditional Animation and computer-based 2D Animation?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "In traditional animation, each picture is drawn by hand on paper, while in 2D computer animation, flat images are created and moved using computer software", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Traditional animation has depth and shadows, while 2D computer animation is completely flat", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Traditional animation is created entirely using block coding, while 2D computer animation is drawn on paper", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "There is no difference; both require drawing 3D models using specialized physical sculpting materials", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["animation", "types", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In electronic spreadsheets, what is AutoFill, and what physical cell feature must you drag to activate it?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "A feature that automatically fills cells with a series of data or copies formulas; you drag the fill handle (small square at the bottom-right corner of the cell)", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "A tool that formats cell colors; you drag the row border", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "A feature that links different sheets together; you double-click the cell grid center", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "A function that inserts circular charts; you drag the formula bar", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "autofill", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'What is cell referencing in an electronic spreadsheet like LibreOffice Calc?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The method of identifying specific cells or ranges of cells using their row and column addresses to help formulas perform calculations accurately", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The process of inserting hyperlinks to external web articles inside cells", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "A formula used to format the font style and size of text data", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "A feature that automatically deletes duplicate number rows in a column", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "referencing", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'Which keyboard shortcut key combination is used in spreadsheet programs to quickly open the dialog box to insert a clickable hyperlink?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Ctrl\\+K", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Ctrl\\+H", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Ctrl\\+D", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Ctrl\\+Z", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "hyperlinks", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'How is Artificial Intelligence (AI) defined in contrast to standard mechanical or electronic machines?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "AI is a type of computer program that can learn from information and make decisions on its own, whereas standard machines only do exactly what they are mechanically or electronically forced to do at that moment", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "AI refers only to physical robots that can walk and speak, whereas standard machines are stationary", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "AI is any computer program that contains mathematical multiplication operations, while standard machines do not", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "AI refers to software programs that can run completely offline without electricity", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["ai_basics", "definitions", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In the field of AI, what does the principle \"Garbage In, Garbage Out\" (GIGO) mean?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "If you train an AI model using incomplete, broken, or biased data, the model will produce incorrect or broken answers", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The AI program will automatically delete files from your Google Drive to clean up space", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "AI systems are only capable of running on computers that are recycled", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "If a computer gets physically dirty, its arithmetic calculations will contain errors", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["machine_mistakes", "data_cleaning", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'Which workspace area inside MIT App Inventor is used by students to drag, drop, and snap together visual code blocks like LEGOs to define the logical behavior of the app?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The Blocks Editor Workspace", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The Designer Workspace Mock-up Screen", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The Components Palette Menu", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The Properties Inspector Panel", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["app_inventor", "blocks_editor", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'According to the Level 3 textbook curriculum, which of the following is considered a core computer component?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Central Processing Unit (CPU)", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Floppy Disk Drive", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Graphics Tablet", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Scanner", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'easy', '["ICT L3: Fundamentals of Computer"]', '["hardware", "auto", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'While online meetings offer several facilities such as being cost-effective and saving travel time, they also have drawbacks. Which of the following is classified as an online meeting drawback in the textbook?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Lack of effective interaction due to the absence of face-to-face communication, which limits reading body language and emotional cues", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The ability to easily schedule and reschedule meetings based on convenience", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The option to record meetings for future reference to help participants review discussions", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Eliminating expenses related to travel, accommodation, and venue booking", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["online_meetings", "drawbacks", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'What is the primary rationale behind the form design tips \"use required fields\" and \"preview before sharing\"?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Required fields make important questions compulsory, and previewing ensures the form is clear, correct, and professional before sending", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Required fields automatically collect email addresses, and previewing saves the form in Google Drive", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Required fields limit responses to one per person, and previewing converts the form into a quiz mode", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Required fields hide unnecessary questions, and previewing translates the form into regional languages", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["online_workspace", "forms_etiquette", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'A student wants to create a YouTube channel to share school learning videos. To sign in and create a channel, which of the following accounts must they possess?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "A Google Account", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "A Microsoft Account", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "A Facebook Account", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "A Yahoo Account", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["social_media", "youtube", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'While YouTube is an excellent platform for watching educational tutorials and sharing learning, it also presents challenges. Which of the following is a recognized disadvantage (con) of YouTube listed in the textbook?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Screen time addiction, inappropriate content, and negative or mean comments", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The cost of subscription is extremely high for basic educational channels", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It only works on desktop computers and cannot be accessed on mobile devices", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It does not allow users to subscribe to their favorite educational channels", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["social_media", "ethics", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In GIMP, how does a text layer differ from standard image layers during the design process?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "It allows the designer to insert and edit text characters dynamically without affecting other parts of the artwork or background layer", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "It cannot be moved, resized, or rotated once it is created on the canvas", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It automatically merges with the background layer, making it impossible to edit later", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It is a non-transparent solid color sheet that covers the entire image size", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["image_editing", "gimp", "text", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'Why are Layer Groups used in complex 2D image design projects that contain a large number of separate layers?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "To keep the workspace neat and organized by grouping layers into a hierarchical structure, allowing multiple layers to be moved, hidden, or modified at once", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "To permanently lock all image layers so that no further edits can be made by the user", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "To reduce the file size of the project by merging all image layers into a single pixel layer", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "To automatically convert 2D raster layers into 3D vector graphics", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["image_editing", "gimp", "layers", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In GIMP, how is a simple 3D drop-shadow text effect created using filters?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "By adding text, navigating to Filters \\(\\rightarrow\\) Light and Shadow \\(\\rightarrow\\) Drop Shadow, and adjusting the offset and blur radius", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "By drawing a square on the workplane and dropping a cylinder inside it", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "By using the Eraser tool to carve a shadow outline on the text layer by hand", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "By adding a Layer Mask and painting it entirely with black brush strokes", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["image_editing", "gimp", "3d_text", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'To make a flat 2D rectangle selection filled with color look like a raised 3D button, what GIMP filter sequence and adjustment should be applied?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Click Filters \\(\\rightarrow\\) Decor \\(\\rightarrow\\) Add Bevel and adjust the thickness parameter as needed", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Click Colors \\(\\rightarrow\\) Brightness-Contrast and maximize the brightness of the rectangle", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Click Layer \\(\\rightarrow\\) New Layer Group and rename the group to \\\"Button\\\"", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Click Edit \\(\\rightarrow\\) Cut and then paste the selection as a new text layer", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["image_editing", "gimp", "3d_shapes", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'Historically, why was hand-drawn traditional animation considered an incredibly big job? Depending on quality, how many frames are typically required for one minute of animation?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Between \\(720\\) and \\(1800\\) separate still images", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Between \\(10\\) and \\(50\\) separate still images", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Exactly \\(100\\) still images", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Over \\(10000\\) still images per second", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["animation", "history", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'When a bouncing rubber ball hits the ground, it squashes flat, and then stretches vertically as it bounces back up. Which fundamental principle of animation does this exemplify?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Squash and Stretch", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Anticipation", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Timing", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Follow Through", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["animation", "principles", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'Before a person jumps, they bend their knees. Before an athlete throws a ball, they pull their arm back. Which animation principle uses a small action before a big action so the audience knows what is coming?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Anticipation", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Ease In and Ease Out", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Timing", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Follow Through", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["animation", "principles", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'According to the animation principle of Timing, how does the number of drawing frames change depending on the speed of an action (e.g., a slow walk vs. a fast run)?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Moving fast requires fewer drawing frames, while moving slowly requires more drawing frames", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Moving fast requires more drawing frames, while moving slowly requires fewer drawing frames", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Both fast and slow movements require the exact same number of drawing frames", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Slow movements do not require any drawing frames; they are done automatically by the software", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["animation", "principles", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'Match the animation software with its description: Which free and open-source software is widely used professionally for 3D modeling, rigging, rendering, and complex 3D animations?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Blender", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Adobe Animate", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Pencil2D", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Microsoft PowerPoint", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["animation", "software", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'What is the default type of cell referencing in spreadsheets, and how does it behave when a formula is copied to another cell?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Relative Referencing; the cell addresses in the formula change automatically relative to where the formula is copied", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Absolute Referencing; the cell addresses remain completely fixed and do not change", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Mixed Referencing; only the column changes while the row remains locked", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Fixed Referencing; the formula is cleared and must be typed again manually", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "referencing", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'A student wants to multiply item prices by a fixed tax rate located in cell B1. They want to copy this formula down the column, ensuring the tax rate cell reference does not change. Which character must they use, and what is the correct absolute reference representation?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The \\$ symbol; represented as \\$B\\$1", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The \\# symbol; represented as \\#B\\#1", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The \\& symbol; represented as \\&B\\&1", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The \\@ symbol; represented as \\@B\\@1", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "referencing", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'A cricket coach records match runs in two different worksheets named Match1 and Match2. To calculate total runs in Sheet3, they want to link B2 from Match1 and B2 from Match2. What is the correct syntax of the linking formula?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "\\=Match1!B2\\+Match2!B2", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "\\=Match1:B2\\+Match2:B2", "correct": true}, {"key": "C", "value": "\\=Match1\\#B2\\+Match2\\#B2", "correct": true}, {"key": "D", "value": "\\=Match1.B2\\+Match2.B2", "correct": true}]', 'D', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'A student records temperature readings hourly throughout the day and wants to visualize how the temperature rises and falls. Which chart type is best suited to show continuous changes or trends in data over a period of time?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Line Chart", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Pie Chart", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Bar Chart", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Histogram", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "charts", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'A company wants to display how its monthly budget is distributed among rent, salaries, utilities, and marketing as percentages of a whole. Which chart type is circular, divided into slices, and has a total slice sum of 100%?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Pie Chart", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Line Chart", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Scatter Chart", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Histogram", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "charts", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'What is the core difference between Supervised Learning and Unsupervised Learning in machine learning models?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Supervised learning uses labeled training data where a teacher gives the correct answers, while unsupervised learning groups unlabeled data on its own by finding patterns", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Supervised learning is only used for text, while unsupervised learning is only used for images", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Supervised learning is performed by humans on paper, while unsupervised learning runs entirely on a computer", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Supervised learning requires constant internet access, while unsupervised learning works completely offline", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["machine_learning", "concepts", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'A school uses an AI program to select students for a sports team. Because past team photos featured mostly tall 8th graders, the AI automatically rejects a fast, highly skilled 6th grader because of their height. Which pillar of AI morals has been violated?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Fairness and Bias", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Privacy", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Accountability", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Transparency", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["ai_ethics", "morals", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'A student writes personal thoughts in a journal app. A week later, they begin seeing targeted advertisements on their phone selling products related to their entries because the app shared their private data. Which moral pillar did this app violate?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Privacy", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Fairness", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Accountability", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Transparency", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["ai_ethics", "privacy", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'A self-driving car confuses a weird shadow and scratches a parked car. The car manufacturer, the software engineers, and the owner sitting in the driver''s seat argue over who is responsible. This represents a central challenge in which ethical pillar?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Accountability", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Transparency", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Fairness", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Privacy", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["ai_ethics", "accountability", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'An AI grading system gives a student a poor grade on a science project. When the student asks why, the teacher replies, \"I have no idea; the computer''s math is a black box we cannot view.\" This failure represents a violation of which AI moral pillar?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Transparency (Explainability)", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Privacy", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Fairness", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Accountability", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["ai_ethics", "transparency", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'Computers do not speak human languages directly. How does Natural Language Processing (NLP) help a school chatbot process a sentence like \"I have a terrible headache today\"?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "It turns the human sentence into math, ignores common filler words, and flags the keyword \\\"headache\\\" to trigger the pre-programmed response", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "It automatically translates the text into binary code and stores it in Google Drive", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It uses a spreadsheet formula to calculate how many characters are in the text", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It opens an online Jitsi Meet video call with a nurse immediately", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["ai_basics", "nlp", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In the MIT App Inventor Designer workspace, what is the primary difference between components like Buttons and Text Labels versus components like Sound players or GPS sensors?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Buttons and Text Labels are Visible components that the user can see and touch on the screen, while Sound players and GPS are Non-Visible components that run in the background", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Buttons and Text Labels cannot be programmed in the Blocks Editor, while Sound players and GPS can", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Non-Visible components appear as colorful visual puzzle pieces on the phone mock-up, while Visible components do not", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Visible components are only used for games, while Non-Visible components are only used for math formulas", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["app_inventor", "components", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'To program a simple app where a picture of a cat plays a \"meow\" sound when tapped, which connected block combination must be built in the Blocks Editor?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "An Event block \\`When Image1.Touched do...\\` containing an Action block \\`Call Sound1.Play\\` inside", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "A text block \\`print(\\\"meow\\\")\\` inside an input function box", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "A mixed referencing formula block \\`=Image1*Sound1\\` from a spreadsheet", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "An absolute referencing block \\`\\$Image\\$1\\` and an \\`unhide\\` block", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["app_inventor", "programming_logic", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'A Prompt Engineer is an emerging career of the AI era. What does a Prompt Engineer do?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Crafts highly specific, structured text instructions and phrasing to talk to AI models to generate the highest quality text, code, or image outputs", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Designs physical mechanical gear components and structural 3D prints in Tinkercad", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Maintains and repairs high-voltage physical hardware lines and circuits in smart factories", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Monitors bank accounts to ensure all automated online loan transactions are completed successfully", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["ai_careers", "prompt_engineering", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In the Level 3 syllabus, which statement best defines the role of communication technology?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Exchanging messages, data, or media electronically over a network", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Printing textual documents in black and white format", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Adding 3D shapes to a slideshow presentation", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Manually adjusting the color levels of an image in GIMP", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'medium', '["ICT L3: Internet and ICT Environment"]', '["communication", "auto", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'What is a Layer Mask in image editing software like GIMP?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "A transparency mask attached to a layer that defines what parts of that layer are transparent or opaque, allowing non-destructive editing", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "A protective tool that prevents any unauthorized users from editing or viewing specific layer details", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "A solid-color background layer that is automatically added when a new file is opened", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "A tool used to draw perfect geometric shapes like circles and rectangles on a text layer", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["image_editing", "gimp", "layer_mask", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'According to the simple rules of Layer Masks, how do the colors black, white, and gray affect layer visibility?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "White shows the layer (full opacity), Black hides the layer (full transparency), and Gray partially hides or blends the layer", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Black shows the layer (full opacity), White hides the layer (full transparency), and Gray has no effect", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "White shows the layer, Gray hides the layer, and Black partially blends the layer", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Gray shows the layer, Black hides the layer, and White makes it fully transparent", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["image_editing", "gimp", "layer_mask", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'What is the key advantage of using a Layer Mask over the Eraser tool in digital art and image blending?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The Eraser tool is destructive because it permanently deletes pixels, while a Layer Mask is non-destructive because pixels are only hidden and can be restored anytime", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The Eraser tool is non-destructive, while a Layer Mask permanently changes the image pixels", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "A Layer Mask is easier for quick permanent cleanup, while the Eraser tool allows for smooth blending", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "There is no functional difference; both permanently delete the original pixels of the image", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["image_editing", "gimp", "layer_mask", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'To create a realistic thick 3D text effect using duplicate layers in GIMP, what steps should a student follow after typing their text?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Duplicate the text layer, change the bottom layer''s color to a darker shade using Brightness-Contrast, and use the Move tool to slightly shift the bottom layer down and right", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Duplicate the text layer, merge it with the background layer, and delete the original text layer", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Duplicate the text layer and apply a black layer mask to the top text layer", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Duplicate the text layer and use the Eraser tool to remove alternate letters from the bottom layer", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Graphics in ICT"]', '["image_editing", "gimp", "3d_text", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In a mixed cell reference such as C\$5 or \$C5, what is the functional effect of the \$ symbol when the formula is copied to other rows or columns?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "It locks and fixes only one part of the cell reference (either the column or the row) while leaving the other part relative", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "It converts the cell value into a currency format with a dollar sign", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It locks both the column and the row simultaneously so neither can change", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It indicates that the cell contains a mathematical formula instead of text", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "referencing", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'Using a spreadsheet to calculate a multiplication table, a student enters the formula \=B\$1\*\$A2 in cell B2. Which type of referencing is being used for both B\$1 and \$A2?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Mixed Referencing", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Relative Referencing", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Absolute Referencing", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Circular Referencing", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "referencing", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'What is the general formula syntax used in LibreOffice Calc to link and pull data from cell B2 in Sheet1 of an external spreadsheet file named \"Match scores.ods\"?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "\\=''file:///path/Match scores.ods''\\#\\$Sheet1.B2", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "\\=[Match scores.ods]Sheet1!B2", "correct": true}, {"key": "C", "value": "\\=Match scores.ods\\#Sheet1:B2", "correct": true}, {"key": "D", "value": "\\=Link(''Match scores.ods'', Sheet1, B2)", "correct": true}]', 'D', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'In a science project, a student wants to plot study hours on the X-axis against student test scores on the Y-axis to see if there is a relationship or correlation between the two. Which chart type plots data points as individual dots using two numerical values?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Scatter (XY) Chart", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Column Chart", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Area Chart", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Histogram", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "charts", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'What are the unique structural features of a Histogram that distinguish it from a standard vertical Column Chart?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "It is used to show the frequency distribution of continuous numerical data grouped into class intervals (ranges) along the X-axis, and the vertical bars touch with no gaps", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "It uses horizontal side-to-side rectangular bars where the length of each bar represents a category ranking", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "It represents values as slices of a circle that must always add up to exactly 100%", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "It connects individual data points with straight lines to show changes over time", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "charts", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'Why might a highly advanced AI system in a self-driving car stop suddenly when encountering a pedestrian''s reflection in a store window, whereas a human driver would easily continue?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The AI lacks common sense and real-world context (context blindness) and relies strictly on mathematical image patterns without understanding reality", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The AI was trying to please the passenger by showing off its braking speed", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The store window reflection was too hot for the car''s temperature sensors", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The AI model suffered a chatbot hallucination and made up a fictional pedestrian", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["machine_mistakes", "context_blindness", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'A student collects school temperature readings: Monday: 32°C, Tuesday: 33°C, Wednesday: -400°C, Thursday: \"Hot\", Friday: 31°C. To clean this dataset before using it to train an AI model, what actions should they take?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "Delete the Wednesday entry (-400°C is physically impossible) and the Thursday entry (\\\"Hot\\\" is a text formatting error) to preserve only valid numeric data", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "Average all five values, including Wednesday and Thursday, to find the median temperature", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "Convert the entire dataset into a Pie chart to automatically hide impossible numbers", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "Convert the text \\\"Hot\\\" into a number 1000 and multiply it by Wednesday''s temperature", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Introduction to AI"]', '["data_science", "data_cleaning", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'If you are linking sheets in LibreOffice Calc, what does the external reference formula \(=Sheet1!B4 + Sheet2!B4\) compute?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The sum of cell B4 in Sheet1 and Sheet2", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The quotient of cell B4 divided by Sheet1", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The product of cell B4 across all active workbooks", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The name of the active worksheet", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "math", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'If you are linking sheets in LibreOffice Calc, what does the external reference formula \(=Sheet2!B4 + Sheet3!B4\) compute?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The sum of cell B4 in Sheet2 and Sheet3", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The quotient of cell B4 divided by Sheet2", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The product of cell B4 across all active workbooks", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The name of the active worksheet", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "math", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'If you are linking sheets in LibreOffice Calc, what does the external reference formula \(=Sheet3!B4 + Sheet4!B4\) compute?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The sum of cell B4 in Sheet3 and Sheet4", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The quotient of cell B4 divided by Sheet3", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The product of cell B4 across all active workbooks", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The name of the active worksheet", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "math", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'If you are linking sheets in LibreOffice Calc, what does the external reference formula \(=Sheet4!B4 + Sheet5!B4\) compute?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The sum of cell B4 in Sheet4 and Sheet5", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The quotient of cell B4 divided by Sheet4", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The product of cell B4 across all active workbooks", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The name of the active worksheet", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "math", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'If you are linking sheets in LibreOffice Calc, what does the external reference formula \(=Sheet5!B4 + Sheet6!B4\) compute?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The sum of cell B4 in Sheet5 and Sheet6", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The quotient of cell B4 divided by Sheet5", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The product of cell B4 across all active workbooks", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The name of the active worksheet", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "math", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'If you are linking sheets in LibreOffice Calc, what does the external reference formula \(=Sheet6!B4 + Sheet7!B4\) compute?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The sum of cell B4 in Sheet6 and Sheet7", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The quotient of cell B4 divided by Sheet6", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The product of cell B4 across all active workbooks", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The name of the active worksheet", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "math", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'If you are linking sheets in LibreOffice Calc, what does the external reference formula \(=Sheet7!B4 + Sheet8!B4\) compute?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The sum of cell B4 in Sheet7 and Sheet8", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The quotient of cell B4 divided by Sheet7", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The product of cell B4 across all active workbooks", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The name of the active worksheet", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "math", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'If you are linking sheets in LibreOffice Calc, what does the external reference formula \(=Sheet8!B4 + Sheet9!B4\) compute?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The sum of cell B4 in Sheet8 and Sheet9", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The quotient of cell B4 divided by Sheet8", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The product of cell B4 across all active workbooks", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The name of the active worksheet", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "math", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'If you are linking sheets in LibreOffice Calc, what does the external reference formula \(=Sheet9!B4 + Sheet10!B4\) compute?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The sum of cell B4 in Sheet9 and Sheet10", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The quotient of cell B4 divided by Sheet9", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The product of cell B4 across all active workbooks", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The name of the active worksheet", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "math", "ict_level3"]', true),
  (sid, cs_id, 'mcq', 'If you are linking sheets in LibreOffice Calc, what does the external reference formula \(=Sheet10!B4 + Sheet11!B4\) compute?', '[{"key": "A", "value": "The sum of cell B4 in Sheet10 and Sheet11", "correct": true}, {"key": "B", "value": "The quotient of cell B4 divided by Sheet10", "correct": false}, {"key": "C", "value": "The product of cell B4 across all active workbooks", "correct": false}, {"key": "D", "value": "The name of the active worksheet", "correct": false}]', 'A', 2, 'hard', '["ICT L3: Electronic Spreadsheet (Extended)"]', '["spreadsheet", "linking", "math", "ict_level3"]', true),
